        <mxCell id="scope" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · Process scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sean Abaniel. This model shows the current appointment process, from a visitor requesting an appointment to the appointment reaching the Next staff team. It covers the roles Visitor, Scheduling, Clinical Operations, Intake and Next staff team. It doesn&#39;t cover new software or a redesigned workflow." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1070" x="45" y="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="walkthrough" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Check the two paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;Incident appointment: steps 1–2, then the held slot is recorded and a booking confirmation is issued, the visitor arrives (step 10), Intake displays “held,” and Dana opens exception review (W05-S04). The booking confirmation and Intake’s held display disagree, and the supplied trace shows no completed readiness decision reaching Intake before arrival. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Evidence and model review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;No complete readiness decision is present in the supplied trace before arrival (W05-S04).The Visitor arrives without any knowledge on whether they will get an appointment or not&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="reflection" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · Learning reflection (reuse your Discord paragraph)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Modelling this process showed me that the booking information and the readiness decision are separate records. It also maps out how Cedar Junction Clinic Appointment system works. But base on the map, the visitor arrives without having a clear knowledge if they will have an appointment or not. This could be an issue for the visitor if they arrive early only to be told that their appointment is actually held. By mapping the process, we can truly identify the problem easily, and providing the solution will be easy work.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1071" x="45" y="525" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="evidence" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=14;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;5 · Portfolio evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[Editable model filename and Week05/Evidence/Week05_Discord_Post.png or .jpg. If Discord is unavailable, identify the equivalent reflection used here.]&lt;br&gt;Save the .drawio file; export both pages as one PDF; check readability; commit and push." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="1070" x="45" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
